# ADR-019 verification obligation: an older long-latency DIV survives a younger
# mispredicted branch and retires. The taken branch is unpredicted (cold BTB), so it
# recovers at execute while the DIV is still in flight; the wrong-path writes to x7 and
# x9 must leave no architectural trace.
@name ooo-div-survives-younger-mispredict
@verifies propOlderSurvivesRecovery funcRobRecovery funcRecoveryKills funcIntegrateExternalDivider
@verifies funcBranchResolve funcMispredictDetect funcBranchRecoveryRequest propRecoveryOnlyOnMispredict
@verifies funcRecoverySelect funcRecoveryPublish propSingleRecoveryPerCycle funcRsRecovery propRsRecoveryKeepsOlder
@verifies funcFetchPcRecovery funcFetchBufferRecovery funcDecodeRecovery funcFuRoute funcIntegrateExternalMultiplier
@maxcycles 4000
li x5, 1000
li x6, 7
li x9, 0
div x7, x5, x6
mul x10, x5, x6
beq x0, x0, correct
addi x7, x0, 1
addi x9, x0, 1
correct: check x7 == 142
check x9 == 0
check x10 == 7000
